          "anchor_id": "cue_s07_c3_flowers_102_average_accuracy_across",
          "text": "On Flowers-102, average accuracy across hue shifts jumps from about thirteen percent for the baseline to thirty-three percent for the fully equivariant model, and similar gains appear on CIFAR-100 and Stanford Cars.",
